-+# Skill Routing Table (Source of Truth)
-+
-+## Precedence Rules
-+1. **Union rule:** When multiple rows match, load the union of required skills. Do not pick a single "best" skill and stop. Both skills are loaded when they apply - precedence only resolves conflicts, it does not suppress loading.
-+2. **Precedence (conflicts only):** `apple-ui` wins on visual tokens, motion values, and data-viz. `designmotion-design` wins on interaction behavior (state coverage, failure modes, pattern choice) where `apple-ui` is silent. If both specify the same thing, `apple-ui` wins and the conflict is noted in the plan.
-+3. **Layering:** `apple-ui` covers how it looks (tokens, color, blur, data-viz, density). `designmotion-design` covers how it behaves (states, timing, failure modes, component system choice). They mostly complement each other.
-+4. **Deterministic first:** Path-based rules beat vague "looks like UI" guesses. Intent-based rules are enforced at plan-time via "Skills consulted".
-+
-+## Routing Rules
-+| Signal (path/keyword/phase) | Required Skills | Conditional | Notes |
-+|---|---|---|---|
-+| Edits under `src/frontend/**` (React/UI components, styling, icons, animation, visible behavior) | `frontend-react`, `apple-ui` | `designmotion-design` if adding/modifying a new screen, form, table, nav, feedback surface, overlay or motion pattern; `browser-verification` at verify step if visible behavior must be proven | This repo is finance-focused. Treat `frontend-react` + `apple-ui` as the pair for any `src/frontend/**` change unless you can justify omitting with a file:line reason. Load both `apple-ui` and `designmotion-design` when either applies - resolve conflicts per precedence rule above. |
-+| Finance keywords: `stock`, `trading`, `crypto`, `portfolio`, `watchlist`, `ticker`, `terminal`, `dark glass fintech`, `market-locale` | `apple-ui` | `frontend-react` if implementing in React; `designmotion-design` if the surface is a new pattern (table, form, nav, overlay, feedback/motion); `browser-verification` for visible behavior | `apple-ui` provides the finance design system. `designmotion-design` is still needed for pattern behavior/states/failure modes on new surfaces. |
-+| General UI pattern/system rules (new screen/form/table/nav/feedback/motion, component states/timing/failure modes) with no strong finance signal | `designmotion-design` | `frontend-react` if implementing; `browser-verification` if visible behavior; `gsd-sketch` if exploratory/throwaway mockups | Mostly dead weight for this repo, but kept for non-finance contexts. The `src/frontend/**` row handles most cases. |
-+| "new/modify endpoint", route/controller/handler for HTTP API | `api-design` | `database-schema-design` if schema touched; `contract-authoring` if request/response/contract shape changes | Follow API design flow before implementation. |
-+| Schema changes (tables/columns/indexes/relations/migrations) | `database-schema-design` | `api-design` if exposed via API | Data layer first. |
-+| Contract changes (OpenAPI/request-response/types) | `contract-authoring` | `api-design` | Keep contracts in sync. |
-+| Multi-module change, new boundary/interface, unclear design depth | `architecture-right-sizing` -> `software-architecture-design` | As needed by impacted areas | Size effort before deep design. |
-+| Any visible-behavior requirement (visual alignment, interaction, responsive, console cleanliness) | `browser-verification` (at verify step) | `frontend-react`/`apple-ui`/`designmotion-design` per area | Prove with real browser evidence (g6). |
-+| Frontend phase needs UI design contract | `gsd-ui-phase` | `apple-ui`, `designmotion-design` as relevant | GSD workflow. |
-+| Audit implemented frontend visually | `gsd-ui-review` | `apple-ui` | GSD workflow. |
-+| UI sketch/exploration | `gsd-sketch` | `designmotion-design` | GSD exploratory. |
-+| Feature requirements work | `requirements-authoring` | `architecture-right-sizing` if non-trivial | Requirements first when unclear. |
-+| AI system phase | `gsd-ai-integration-phase` | `software-architecture-design` as needed | GSD workflow. |
